 { With a superior pawn structure and more active king, there is not doubt as to White's advantage, but how to progress? } 1. { -KEY- } Bxc4 $1 { A good exchange in order to help the king approach the battlefield. } dxc4 2. Ke3 Rd3+ ( { Or } 2... Rg4 3. Rf2 $1 { with the threat of Rf4 - De Dovitiis. } ) 
3. Ke4 Kg7 4. Rxc4 Rd2 5. b4 $1 { Of course - betting on the passed pawn. } axb4 6. axb4 Rxh2 7. Kd5 { Already at this point, White should prepare himself for a future rook vs. pawn (s) ending - Valerga. } Rg2 8. Rg4+ ( 8. Rc3 { was more practical - De Dovitiis. } ) 
Kf6 9. b5 h5 10. Rf4+ Ke7 11. Rf3 Rb2 ( { Or } 11... Kd8 12. Kc6 Kc8 13. Rxf7 Rc2 14. Kb6 Rc3 15. Rg7  { with } 16. Rg8 { next, in similar fashion to the previous example. } ) 
12. Kc6 Rc2+ 13. Kb7 Ke6 ( 13... Rc4 $1 { was more tenacious, preparing h5-h4, when White would have to find } 14. b6 h4 15. gxh4 Rxh4 16. Rf5 $1 { cutting off the king from the fifth rank in advance; e.g. } Ke6 17. Ra5 f5 18. Ka7 { etc. } ) 
14. b6 f5 15. Ra3 $1 { Creating a shelter for the king on a7. } Rb2 16. Ka7 f4 17. gxf4 Kf5 18. Ra5+ ( { After } 18. Ra5 Kg4 19. Rg5 { Black's counterplay is over, so he resigned. } ) 

